Architecture plan for mike-t-302f-test-website-005

Product and app shape
- Product name: mike-t-302f-test-website-005.
- The app is a Vite + React + TypeScript single-page landing page for an "Agent Team for Founders" offer.
- Future implementation should keep all copy product-driven and editable through shared content data, not hardcoded throughout presentational components.

Module structure and file organization
- src/main.tsx: React bootstrap only.
- src/App.tsx: top-level composition of the landing page shell and sections.
- src/index.css: Tailwind imports, base layer, global page styles, and smooth scrolling.
- src/config/env.ts: typed build-time env accessor for values such as VITE_CTA_URL.
- src/content/siteContent.ts: single editable content source for nav items, hero copy, SDLC steps, feature cards, benefits, FAQ items, CTA labels, and footer copy.
- src/types/content.ts: shared content contracts such as NavItem, HeroContent, StepItem, FeatureItem, BenefitItem, FAQItem, and SiteContent.
- src/components/ui/: reusable primitives including Button, Section, Card, and AccordionItem.
- src/components/layout/: AppShell, Header/Nav, and Footer.
- src/components/sections/: Hero, HowItWorks, Features, FounderBenefits, and FAQ.
- src/lib/: small shared helpers only when needed, such as class name merging.

Dependencies between issues
- Issue #3 should land first because Tailwind and design tokens define the styling contract for every UI issue.
- Issue #4 can run in parallel with #3 after the initial app exists; env access is required before wiring CTAs.
- Issue #5 should follow #3/#4 so content and env-aware CTA data can be typed cleanly.
- Issue #6 depends on #3 and should use the design tokens without owning product copy.
- Issue #7 depends on #5 and #6 because the shell needs nav/footer content and reusable buttons/sections.
- Issue #8 depends on #4, #5, and #6 because the hero uses content data, the CTA URL, and UI primitives.
- Issues #9, #10, and #11 depend on #5 and #6 because they render typed content through cards/sections.
- Issue #12 depends on #5 and #6 because FAQ content should come from the content module and use AccordionItem.

Key design decisions
- Keep components presentational and data-driven; section components should receive or import typed content rather than duplicating copy.
- Centralize brand tokens in Tailwind theme configuration and map them to semantic names such as brand, surface, text, border, accent, and muted.
- Prefer simple React state for the FAQ accordion; no routing or state library is needed for this single-page landing page.
- Use anchor IDs for sections and nav links so the layout shell can support smooth in-page navigation without adding a router.
- Keep CTA behavior behind the typed env accessor so missing or malformed VITE_CTA_URL fails predictably during development.
- Use accessible HTML first: semantic sections, real buttons/links, visible focus styles, aria-expanded on accordion triggers, and heading order that matches page structure.
- Do not introduce broad abstractions beyond the listed UI primitives until repeated section implementation shows a concrete need.
